==Strategy==
The main difficulty in this stage obviously comes from surviving the wave of Gabriels and Haterbaas that appear upon base hit. Ramen Cat can do a good job of holding the enemies back, and strong attackers like Pizza Cat or Mushroom Cat can deal huge chunks of damage to the Gabriels. Critters like Catasaurus and Catornado will make short work of the Haterbaas.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Li'l Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Macho Cat]]: While Li'l Macho Cat is essentially a generic Cat clone, they have a [[Cat Combo]] with Catasaurus, which is another unit you're highly likely to bring here. Plus, their [[True Form]] gains a lower cost, and even the ability to occasionally land a [[Critical Hit]] through [[Talents]], which can help greatly since the Haterbaas have low enough health to be killed by it.
*[[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]]: Catasaurus is a basic but good Critter, and as mentioned previously, has a [[Mini-Saurus (Combo)|research Combo]] with Li'l Cat which is worth bringing here.
*[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]]: Ramen Cat is an obvious choice for a meatshield, as they have resistance against the Gabriels and Angelic Hippoes, and can even survive a hit from the Haterbaas in Lv.20 if at Lv.50+11 (or Lv.50 with max Defense Talent).
*[[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]]: Can deal with the horde of Gabriels that spawn on base hit very well thanks to its Area Attack. Plus, it has high enough range that it shouldn't be hit by Haterbaas.
*[[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]]: Although he requires you to beat [[Fury of Hell (Merciless)|Fury of Hell]], once unlocked he can be used as a ranged Critter. His fast attack rate make him one of the best units to bring here.

